      "writtenOn": "2024-07-23T07:44:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should probably be a separate extension. Because explicit resolve will need a separate render pass and require storing/loading the MSAA texture to/from memory. This is not desired on tiled based GPUs such as Apple Silicon.\n\nBy separating this into its own extension, we can enable it for D3D11 and disable it on Metal if Apple GPU is detected for example, and think about implementation on Metal \u0026 vulkan later. Bonus: We can disable it on Arm Windows as well.\n\nCorentin and Austin might have different opinions. But in general, I think this is not an universal feature that should be enabled to every GPU.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 8,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "129f47db61d1a5490233e5078da7bdf093d29a57",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
